       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day, which is about 5 times the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual outpatient maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and the OTC maximum is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n\n- **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day), a common dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation\n- **800 mg** by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum dose\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note."
